# SpecDD kitchen sink fixture.
# Whole-line comments are allowed; inline trailing comments are intentionally absent.

Spec: SpecDD Kitchen Sink Fixture

Platform: SpecDD/1.2

Purpose:
  Exercise every documented SpecDD section and common syntax form in one valid fixture.
  Provide a compact reference file for readers, examples, syntax highlighting, and parser smoke tests.

Structure:
  kitchen-sink.sdd: Complete language coverage fixture
  generated: Optional generated outputs for local experiments
  generated/*.json: Machine-readable coverage snapshots
  examples/sample.js: JavaScript path token sample
  examples/sample.ts: TypeScript path token sample
  examples/component.tsx: TSX path token sample
  examples/component.jsx: JSX path token sample
  examples/tool.py: Python path token sample
  examples/service.go: Go path token sample
  examples/lib.rs: Rust path token sample
  examples/App.java: Java path token sample
  examples/Program.cs: C# path token sample
  examples/model.rb: Ruby path token sample
  examples/page.php: PHP path token sample
  examples/schema.json: JSON path token sample
  examples/config.yaml: YAML path token sample
  examples/config.yml: YML path token sample
  examples/site.toml: TOML path token sample
  examples/styles.css: CSS path token sample
  examples/index.html: HTML path token sample

Owns:
  kitchen-sink.sdd
  generated/*
  SpecDDKitchenSink
  KitchenSinkCoverageReport
  Coverage fixture authorship and maintenance

Can modify:
  kitchen-sink.sdd
  generated/*

Can read:
  ../README.md
  ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.md
  ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.project.md
  ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.local.md
  ../web/assets/js/specdd-highlight.js

References:
  ../README.md
  ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.md
  ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.project.md
  ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.local.md

Must:
  Include every currently documented SpecDD section label.
  Include at least one whole-line comment.
  Include path examples, glob examples, symbol examples, and free-form prose examples.
  Include all documented task states.
  Keep references pointed at files that exist in this repository.
  Remain readable as a single source-adjacent development contract.

Must not:
  Require implementation files outside tmp to change.
  Use inline trailing comments.
  Treat examples as permission to ignore inherited SpecDD bootstrap rules.
  Expand write authority beyond the paths listed in Can modify.

Forbids:
  ../src/**
  ../web/**
  network access
  destructive filesystem commands
  undocumented task state markers

Depends on:
  README.md
  src/.specdd/bootstrap.md
  SpecDD bootstrap language
  SpecDDKitchenSink.coverageMatrix()
  SpecDDKitchenSink.ReportBuilder.build(input)

Exposes:
  tmp/kitchen-sink.sdd
  SpecDDKitchenSink.coverageMatrix()
  SpecDDKitchenSink.ReportBuilder.build(input)
  KitchenSinkCoverageReport.sections

Accepts:
  SpecDD version 1.2 section vocabulary
  relative paths
  glob paths
  task status markers
  Gherkin-like scenario steps
  small concrete examples

Returns:
  a complete kitchen sink .sdd fixture
  a human-readable coverage contract
  parser and highlighter smoke-test input
  KitchenSinkCoverageReport

Raises:
  MissingSectionCoverageError
  MissingTaskStateCoverageError
  InvalidInlineCommentError
  MissingReferenceError

Handles:
  root-relative mental model from tmp
  sibling and parent path references
  task state coverage
  Given steps
  When steps
  Then steps
  And steps
  But steps

Tasks:
  [x] #0 Include identity sections.
  [x] #1 Include scope and ownership sections.
  [x] #2 Include positive and negative constraint sections.
  [x] #3 Include interface and contract sections.
  [x] #4 Include workflow and behavior sections.
  [ ] #5 Use this fixture in future parser or documentation checks.
  [!] #6 Add automated validation when official validation tooling exists.
  [?] #7 Decide whether fixtures should include intentionally invalid examples in a separate file.
  [-] #8 Skip implementation changes because this request only creates a spec fixture.
  # This indented comment is still a comment and is not a task.

Done when:
  Every documented section label appears at least once.
  Every documented task state appears at least once.
  Scenarios include Given, When, Then, And, and But steps.
  References resolve to existing files.
  The fixture remains a single .sdd file under tmp.

Scenario: every documented section is represented
  Given the SpecDD language defined by README.md and src/.specdd/bootstrap.md
  And this fixture is read from top to bottom
  When a reader checks the section labels
  Then Spec, Platform, Purpose, Structure, Owns, Can modify, Can read, References, Must, Must not, Forbids, Depends on, Exposes, Accepts, Returns, Raises, Handles, Tasks, Done when, Scenario, and Example are present
  But no inline trailing comment is required to understand the fixture

Scenario: task states are covered
  Given the allowed task states are open, done, skipped, blocked, and needs decision
  And optional numeric task IDs may be present
  When the Tasks section is scanned
  Then [ ], [x], [-], [!], and [?] are all represented
  And task IDs such as #0 and #8 are visible

Scenario: write authority remains local
  Given this fixture owns kitchen-sink.sdd and generated/*
  When an agent works under this spec
  Then only kitchen-sink.sdd and generated/* may be modified
  And ../README.md and ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.md may be read as context
  But ../src/** and ../web/** remain forbidden modification targets

Example:
  input spec path: tmp/kitchen-sink.sdd
  reference path: ../src/.specdd/bootstrap.md
  glob path: generated/*.json
  public symbol: SpecDDKitchenSink.ReportBuilder.build(input)
  accepted task states: [ ] [x] [-] [!] [?]
  accepted scenario words: Given When Then And But
  output file: generated/coverage.json
  output status: complete
